.TH PAPERWEIGHT\-SECRETS\-SYNC 1 "2026-07-16" "paperweight-secrets 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
paperweight\-secrets\-sync \- mirror pass(1) entries into pass\-secret\-service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B paperweight\-secrets\-sync
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR pass\-secret\-service (1)
only exposes secrets that were created through its own D\-Bus API; it does
not know about entries added directly with
.BR pass (1).
.B paperweight\-secrets\-sync
bridges that gap in one direction: it mirrors every regular pass(1) entry
into a dedicated
.I secret_service/cli_mirror
collection as a symlink back to the real
.I .gpg
file, alongside a synthesized
.I .properties
sidecar giving it a readable
.I Label
(the original pass(1) path). Nothing is copied or re\-encrypted.
.PP
Mirror entries whose source has since been deleted are removed (both the
symlink and its
.IR .properties ).
.PP
.BR pass\-secret\-service (1)
scans its store once at startup, so this script restarts the
.I dbus\-org.freedesktop.secrets.service
systemd user unit at the end (best\-effort; a no\-op if nothing was running,
since D\-Bus activation covers first use anyway).
.PP
Safe to re\-run at any time \(em existing mirrors are left alone unless
their source disappeared. Suitable for a cron job or systemd timer.
.PP
The reverse direction needs no syncing:
.BR paperweight\-passmenu (1)
already reads app\-created secrets' labels directly.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.password-store/secret_service/cli_mirror/
Mirror collection created and maintained by this script.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pass (1),
.BR paperweight\-passmenu (1),
.BR paperweight\-secrets\-init (1)
